ore than a village.<br>5. castelli and castra10-100 inhabitants: <i>castelli</i> and <i>castra</i>: These were nucleated settlements, surrounded by a circuit wall, that originated in 10th- and 11th-century efforts to control agricultural surpluses and peasant production, often by monasteries such as Farfa. Examples from Lazio in this period include Tusculo.<br>Although there were some fortified settlements (<i>oppida</i>) in Lazio before the 10th century, castles begin to appear in the documents from the 930s: Montorio was founded in 934, Bocchignano in 939. Wickham stresses the degree to which these foundations required detailed planning and substantial demographic shifts, since these new foundations had to be populated from the surrounding area.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1072, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 903})
