tants in 1718;70,964 inhabitants in 1791)<br>3. towns: Provincial centers such as Perugia (which contained around 17,385 people in 1656 and 13,997 people in 1736 served as administrative centers for provincial government.<br>4. villages: Market towns such as Norcia, with 2146 residents in 1736 Ancona, which held 20,000 people in the mid-seventeenth century, had declined to about 7,000 inhabitants around 1700, following papal suppression of religious and ethnic minorities there.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 999, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 788})
