 which together had a population of around 12,292 people)3. Tertiary centres (including new medium-sized settlements on the piedmont, such as Rancho Tejas, Sta. Cruz Mixtepec and "El Choco" near Ayoquezco)4. Small villages and hamlets (hundreds of small hamlets were present but are less well represented)<br>"Table 7.9. Monte Alban IIIA population hierarchy in Oaxaca and Ejuta."<br>Vallay of Oaxaca: Level I: 12835-16507; II: 4925-6195; III: 1789-3219: IV: 715-1575; V: 211-608; VI: 116-197. No rank: 8-100.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1015, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 880})
